# BOHEMIA ACT ONE ASK -- PLAYABLE .bq (canon machine layer)
# A01 -- THE KILLING SUMMER
#
# HIS RULING, 7/19, LOCKED: the ten opening options not used in the cold open
# become THE FIRST ACT ONE QUESTS. "Nothing is wasted; the menu of openings is
# really the menu of early Act 1 content." Seven of the ten had never been
# written anywhere. This is one of them, and its line is his own:
#   "THE KILLING SUMMER -- no enemy but the desert; brownout heat peaks, the
#    die-off crests, you choose who gets water and who does not."
#
# THE ASK IS A CLAIM, AND A CLAIM IS CHECKED BY GOING TO THE THING. Of 158
# measured deception cues 118 mean nothing, pauses among them, and people catch
# lies 47% of the time. THE LIAR IS BELIEVED, and nothing in his mouth is a tell.
# So there is no [READ] option here, no skill roll and no highlighted "he's
# lying" line: he says the block above is taking more than its share, and the
# only way to know is to walk up there and look at the pressure yourself.
#
# AND IT CHANGES SOMETHING VISIBLE, which is the whole difference between an ask
# and filler: water moves, and the block that gets it stops being the block that
# does not.
#
# NO CLOCK. His element line has a die-off cresting and the obvious build is a
# failable timer. The study on that is blunt: a hard clock alienates, the water
# chip timer frustrated players and the sequel removed it. The pressure here is
# that somebody goes without either way, which is his own sentence, not a bar
# emptying on screen.
#
# draft:true. Every line is an attempt and not one word is approved.

# ---- QUESTBOOK STUDY CITATIONS (QUEST STUDY LAW, 7/26/26) -------------------
# @STUDY Q033.W4  DEMONSTRATED, NOT TOLD (the mechanical proof)
#   applied: nobody tells you the upstream block is drawing more; you walk to the standpipe and the pressure is the proof, so the mechanic carries the claim instead of a line of dialogue.
# @STUDY Q026.W5  ACCUSE-WHO-YOU-BELIEVE *OR* WHO-DESERVES-IT
#   applied: the fork is not who is lying, it is who goes without, so truth and justice come apart exactly the way his own line says they do.
# @STUDY Q038.X1  THE HARD CLOCK ALIENATES (F1
#   applied: the die-off is the setting and not a failable timer, because the named failure of the water chip clock is that it alienates, so the pressure here is who suffers rather than how long you have.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

@QUEST   bq_a01_the_killing_summer   The Killing Summer
@ACT     1
@FACTION NONE
@ONCE    true

@ROLE keeper   REQ  block=same
@ROLE upstream OPT  block=other

@STAGE 10
  @LOG Hottest week anybody remembers and our standpipe is down to a dribble by noon.
  @DO show_objective 10
@STAGE 20
  @LOG Walked up the line myself. He was right about the pressure and wrong about why.
  @DO show_objective 20
  @DO complete_objective 10
@STAGE 30 COMPLETE #quiet
  @LOG Split it. Neither block gets what it needs and both blocks get through the week.
  @DO pay resources 1
  @DO set_flag summer_split
  @DO learn pressure_is_the_proof
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 31 COMPLETE #notable
  @LOG Gave it to us and said so out loud. They know who did it and they know why.
  @DO pay resources 1
  @DO set_flag summer_took_ours
  @DO learn pressure_is_the_proof
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 32 COMPLETE #risky
  @LOG Gave it upstream. Our people watched me do it and nobody has said a word to me since.
  @DO pay resources 1
  @DO set_flag summer_gave_it_up
  @DO learn pressure_is_the_proof
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 33 FAIL #quiet
  @LOG Left the valve where it was. The heat did the choosing instead of me.

@OBJ 10  "Find out why the pressure drops"  target=keeper
@OBJ 20  "Decide who gets the water"         target=keeper

# =====================================================================
# THE CLAIM. He states it flat and he may be wrong. Nothing in the scene
# tells you which, because nothing in a face ever does.
# =====================================================================
@TALK claim  speaker=keeper  entry=stage>=10
  @SAY By noon this pipe is spitting air and by three there is nothing. Third day running. #tired
  @SAY The block above us is drawing more than their share. I am not guessing, I am telling you.
  @SAY Go up and look at their standpipe yourself. Then come back and tell me I am wrong.
  @OPT "How do you know?"           [gate: none]  -> how
  @OPT "I'll go and look."          [gate: none]  -> walk
  @OPT "Say they are. Then what?"   [gate: none]  -> then
  @OPT (go, without answering)      [gate: none]  SILENCE -> walk
  @NOVERB "Are you lying to me?"
@END

@TALK how  speaker=keeper
  @SAY I do not, not the way you mean. I know what my own pipe does and I know it did not do this last summer. #tired
  @SAY That is the whole of what I have. Which is why I am asking you to go instead of arguing with me.
  @OPT "Then I'll go."              [gate: none]  -> walk
  @OPT "Say they are. Then what?"   [gate: none]  -> then
@END

@TALK then  speaker=keeper
  @SAY Then somebody goes without, and it is either them or it is us, and I would rather it was them. #dread
  @SAY I am not going to pretend that is a nice thing to want.
  @OPT "I'll look first."           [gate: none]  -> walk
  @OPT (say nothing)                [gate: none]  SILENCE -> walk
@END

@TALK walk  speaker=keeper
  @SAY Straight up the line. You will hear it before you see it. #tired
  @DO set_stage 20
@END

# =====================================================================
# THE FENCE. The pressure is the proof, and it does not say what he said.
# =====================================================================
@TALK standpipe  speaker=upstream  entry=stage>=20
  @SAY You are the third one up here this week and I will tell you what I told them. #wary
  @SAY Feel it. Ours is worse than yours. Whatever is happening is happening above both of us and neither of us has the reach to go and look at it.
  @SAY So the only thing left to decide is who gets what is coming down. That is not a lie, that is a valve.
  @OPT "Then we split it."          [gate: none]  -> split
  @OPT "Then it comes to us."       [gate: none]  -> ours
  @OPT "Then keep it."              [gate: none]  -> theirs
  @OPT (stand there and think)      [gate: none]  SILENCE -> split
  @NOVERB "Go up and find out who is taking it"
@END

@TALK split  speaker=upstream
  @SAY Half a week each and both of us thirsty. That is the honest one and it is nobody's favourite. #tired
  @OPT (set it that way)            [gate: none]  SILENCE -> END  @DO set_stage 30
  @OPT "No. Ours."                  [gate: none]  -> ours
@END

@TALK ours  speaker=upstream
  @SAY Then say it where my people can hear you say it, because they are going to ask me who decided. #dread
  @OPT (say it in front of them)    [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 31
  @OPT "Split it instead."          [gate: none]  -> split
@END

@TALK theirs  speaker=upstream
  @SAY You are going to have to walk back down and tell your own people that. #wary
  @OPT (walk back down)             [gate: none]  SILENCE -> END  @DO set_stage 32
  @OPT "Split it instead."          [gate: none]  -> split
  @OPT (leave the valve alone)      [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 33
@END
